1. Scope and inspection

This license covers the Despia-authored extension source code, examples and
associated documentation in this repository (the Software). Anyone with lawful
access may read, inspect and download the Software and keep inspection copies or
GitHub forks under section 4. The Software is proprietary and source available.

2. Development, evaluation and testing

Anyone with lawful access may copy, modify, build and run the Software for
development, evaluation and testing with a Despia V3 app. No paid Despia
license is required for this noncommercial use. You may install test builds
on your devices and share test builds with people testing the app for you.
You may develop and test an app you intend to release commercially later.

This grant covers development and testing only. You need the applicable
license under section 3 before using the Software in a production release,
operating it commercially or using it to generate revenue.

3. Commercial use in a licensed application

To use the Software commercially or deploy it in production, you must hold
a valid Despia commercial license and maintain a valid Despia project for
the particular application. The license must cover the operating system on
which you deploy the Software.

A Despia Solo Pack covers one application on its licensed operating system,
iOS or Android. A Despia Hybrid Pack covers one application on both iOS and
Android. An existing applicable Despia license includes use of all Despia V3
extension templates you have lawful access to. No separate extension purchase
or per-extension fee applies. You may also build and use any number of your
own extensions for the licensed application and operating system.

Subject to these conditions, Despia grants you a non-exclusive license to copy,
modify and build the Software into that application's Despia V3 runtime and
distribute and operate that application for its end users. End users may run
the extension as part of your licensed application without buying a separate
developer license. A license for one application does not cover another.
A separate written agreement with Despia may provide different terms.

